        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"MigrantP\"]\n\nAh I see, I thought that each team would play the same game and see who could win (or win the quickest).To make it interesting, have each team choose the heroes for the other ;)\n\n[/quote]\n\nMaybe, but if one team is picking both the villain and the heroes, what is the other team actually doing?\n\n&nbsp;\n\nImagine, though, that your opponent has chosen a villain for you to face and you can choose any heroes. You take an awesome team. Great! But what happens later when you get to the fourth round and you&#39;ve gone through your 12 favorite heroes. Then what? There would be a lot of having to decide how many rounds you think you can make it.\n\nLikewise, you could assign Iron Legacy right off the bat, but if you do that, your opponent may pick the strongest set of heroes to face him. Maybe you&#39;d like to wait a few rounds before assigning Iron Legacy?\n",
